sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Caller knowledge can lag the actual outcome
  accDescr: A caller submits attempt R. The service confirms R but its response is lost. The caller times out and knows only that R is unresolved to it, while the service remains confirmed. Later the caller asks for the outcome of R and learns it was confirmed. No second reservation is created by this conceptual reconciliation.
  participant C as Caller
  participant S as Service
  C->>S: Submit attempt R
  S->>S: Confirm R
  S--xC: Confirmation lost
  Note over C,S: Caller: unknown<br/>Service: confirmed
  C->>C: Timeout, stop waiting
  C->>S: Ask outcome of R
  S-->>C: R is confirmed
  Note over C,S: Caller now knows confirmed


